<title>ISRAEL: Tadiran Telecom gets $10 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Tadiran Telecom gets $10 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tadiran Telecommunications said it was awarded a $10 million contract by Telecommunications of Jamaica for the supply of wireless local loop systems.</p>
<p>Telecommunications of Jamaica is 75 percent owned by Cable &amp; Wireless Plc.</p>
<p>Separately, the Israeli company said its local loop system was being used to connect subscribers to Atlantic Telecom's new telecommunications network in Glasgow, Scotland.</p>
<p>The equipment is part of an agreement signed between the two companies at the end of 1995. According to this agreement, Atlantic Telecom will exclusively base its new telecommunications on Tadiran Telecom's access system.</p>
<p>Tadiran Telecom is a subsidiary of Tadiran Ltd.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
